  As I posted earlier, I have successfully compiled Nethack 3.0 with a pretty
good collection of features using Microsoft C 5.1.  Here is how I did it:

First, the following are defined in config.h:

SPELLS, POLYSELF, THRONES, HARD, FOUNTAINS, MEDUSA, NAMED_ITEMS, ARMY,
THEOLOGY, SOUNDS, ELBERETH, WORM, ALTARS, WALLIFIED_MAZE, MUSIC, TOLKIEN

the ones left out are: PROBING, REDO, WALKIES, KOPS, COM_COMP, SHIRT,
SINKS, REINCARNATION, ORACLE, EXPLORE_MODE, SEDUCE, STRONGHOLD, GOLEMS,
KICK, TUTTI_FRUTTI

of course, you are free to exchange things at will.  I just tried to pick
as many of the ones I wanted as possible.  

The final size of the EXE files is 576579 - and I really don't think you
can get any bigger easily.  I use DOS 3.3 with BUFFERS=5 and FILES=5 when
I run Nethack 3.0 - this doesn't seem to hurt the game.  If you run DOS 4.0,
this file is too big and you will have to cut out options.

I also compiled the game with 80186 code generation on - if you don't have
a V-20, 80286,  or up (i.e., stuck with an 8088), then you will probably
have to take out something because of size.

I used NDMake to run the Makefile - it may work with other Make programs
also, but I didn't bother trying.

I don't think I had to make ANY changes to the source code at all - it 
compiled cleanly.  Here is the Makefile I used, which I changed quite
a bit from the original.  (Maybe this could get included in future
editions?  The one they give for Microsoft C is really useless.)
After the Makefile is the make.ini file (used with NDMake).

